que_le_clique:conclusion:Lax496464.WH_D12_MulticolouredClique.multicolouredClique_le_clique:0","e:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.W1Derived.multicolouredClique_W1_complete:assumption:Lax496464.WH_D12_MulticolouredClique.multicolouredClique_le_clique:0"],"kind":"dock","label":"WH_D12_MulticolouredClique.multicolouredClique_le_clique","nodeId":"c:Lax496464.WH_D12_MulticolouredClique","semanticId":"Lax496464.WH_D12_MulticolouredClique.multicolouredClique_le_clique"},"p:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Parameters.multicolouredClique_isParameterized":{"href":"../lax-496464/Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Parameters.multicolouredClique_isParameterized.html","incident":["e:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Parameters.multicolouredClique_isParameterized:assumption:Lax496464.WH_A5_Bridges:0","e:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Parameters.multicolouredClique_isParameterized:conclusion:Lax496464.WH_D12_MulticolouredClique.multicolouredClique_isParameterized:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"","nodeId":"p:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Parameters.multicolouredClique_isParameterized","semanticId":"Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Parameters.multicolouredClique_isParameterized"},"p:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Reductions.CliqueMCC.ForgetFinal.multicolouredClique_le_clique":{"href":"../lax-496464/Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Reductions.CliqueMCC.ForgetFinal.multicolouredClique_le_clique.html","incident":["e:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Reductions.CliqueMCC.ForgetFinal.multicolouredClique_le_clique:assumption:Lax496464.WH_A5_Bridges:0","e:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Reductions.CliqueMCC.ForgetFinal.multicolouredClique_le_clique:conclusion:Lax496464.WH_D12_MulticolouredClique.multicolouredClique_le_clique:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"**Multicoloured Clique ≤fpt p-Clique.** Forget the colours: the word keeps its graph block and its\nlast entry, the number of colours. A clique of `k` vertices in a properly `k`-coloured graph has one\nvertex of each colour, and a multicoloured clique is a `k`-clique; the parameter is unchanged, and\nthe map is computed in linear time.","nodeId":"p:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Reductions.CliqueMCC.ForgetFinal.multicolouredClique_le_clique","semanticId":"Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Reductions.CliqueMCC.ForgetFinal.multicolouredClique_le_clique","tooltipHtml":"<strong>Multicoloured Clique ≤fpt p-Clique.</strong> Forget the colours: the word keeps its graph block and its\nlast entry, the number of colours. A clique of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span> vertices in a properly <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span>-coloured graph has one\nvertex of each colour, and a multicoloured clique is a <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span>-clique; the parameter is unchanged, and\nthe map is computed in linear time."},"p:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Reductions.CliqueMCC.ProdFinal.clique_le_multicolouredClique":{"href":"../lax-496464/Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Reductions.CliqueMCC.ProdFinal.clique_le_multicolouredClique.html","incident":["e:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Reductions.CliqueMCC.ProdFinal.clique_le_multicolouredClique:assumption:Lax496464.WH_A5_Bridges:0","e:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Reductions.CliqueMCC.ProdFinal.clique_le_multicolouredClique:conclusion:Lax496464.WH_D12_MulticolouredClique.clique_le_multicolouredClique:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"**p-Clique ≤fpt Multicoloured Clique.** For `k ≤ n`, take `k` copies of the vertex set, the copy\n`c` coloured `c`, and join `(c, u)` and `(c', v)` when `c ≠ c'` and `uv` is an edge; a\nmulticoloured clique picks `k` distinct pairwise adjacent vertices, and conversely. For `k > n`\nthe word of a fixed no-instance (one colour, no vertices) is written. The number of colours is at\nmost `k`, and the map is computed in polynomial time.","nodeId":"p:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Reductions.CliqueMCC.ProdFinal.clique_le_multicolouredClique","semanticId":"Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Reductions.CliqueMCC.ProdFinal.clique_le_multicolouredClique","tooltipHtml":"<strong>p-Clique ≤fpt Multicoloured Clique.</strong> For <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k ≤ n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8304em;vertical-align:-0.136em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span>,